

Page 1 of 12
Partner Service Agreement
1. Parties and definitions
1.1  This Partner Service Agreement ("Agreement") is between Owen Holdeman, an individual doing business as
Ghostwright Web Development, an Arizona sole proprietorship ("Ghostwright"), and the business named as
Partner in Exhibit B ("Partner"), effective on the date Ghostwright confirms receipt of Partner's signed copy under
Section 16.8 ("Effective Date").
1.2  In this Agreement:
Client means a business that Partner serves and for which Partner orders a Site.
Site means a website that Ghostwright builds and hosts for a Client under this Agreement.
Intake means the completed intake form for the Client's business, hosted on a subdomain of Partner's
website.
Greenlight means the moment Ghostwright holds both a complete Intake and payment in full of the Setup
Fee for a Site.
Approval means Partner's written approval of a Site version, or a version treated as approved under Section
4.4.
Go-Live means the Site is complete and publicly available on the Client's own domain.
Billing Start Date means the earlier of Go-Live or, if launch is delayed more than 14 days after Approval for
reasons outside Ghostwright's control, the 15th day after Approval.
Active Site means a Site that has reached its Billing Start Date and has not been cancelled.
Business Day means Monday to Friday, excluding U.S. federal holidays.
Setup Fee and Monthly Fee mean the fees in Exhibit A.
Cancellation Notice Date means the date Ghostwright receives Partner's written notice cancelling a Site.
Cancellation Date means the last day of the calendar month that contains the Cancellation Notice Date.
Buyout Window and Buyout Steps have the meanings in Section 11.
Source Code has the meaning in Section 11.8.
Launch Checklist means the short email Ghostwright sends Partner under Section 5.5, listing the tests it
ran and the results.
Ghostwright-Caused Form Failure has the meaning in Section 8.14.
2. Services and scope
2.1  Ghostwright will design, build, host, and maintain each Site on a white-label basis, under Partner's brand, for
Partner's Clients.
2.2  Each Site includes:
•
custom design and code written from scratch, with no templates, page builders, or reused starter code;
•
a mobile-responsive layout;
•
a dedicated page for each major service the Client offers, with smaller related services grouped on the
same page;
•
contact forms that use EmailJS, set up as described in Section 8;
•
SEO-ready structure and meta tags; and
Partner Service Agreement, Version 1.2
