•
hosting and SSL.
2.3  Not included, and quoted separately: new features and integrations (other than the simple tracking described
in Section 8.4), e-commerce, additional major service pages after launch, redesigns, and third-party subscriptions
or tools.
2.4  Partner sets its own prices, bills its Clients, and owns the Client relationship. Ghostwright bills only Partner.
2.5  Ghostwright may use subcontractors and third-party services (such as hosting and form tools) but remains
responsible for its own performance.
2.6  There is no minimum volume, and neither party is required to work exclusively with the other.
2.7  Images. Ghostwright may use licensed stock images and AI-assisted tools to prepare images for a Site,
within the choices the Client makes in the Intake. Ghostwright may improve the quality of images and logos the
Client supplies, such as sharpening, brightening, cropping, resizing, converting file types, and cleaning up minor
flaws, but will not change what an image shows. Ghostwright will not present a generated image as a photo of a
Client's completed work, team, or customers, and will not create reviews or testimonials. Generated and stock
images are licensed for use on the Site, are not exclusive to the Client, and are not covered by Section 13.7.
2.8  Ghostwright manages each Site and makes all edits to it while it is in service. Partner and the Client do not
receive administrative access to the Site or to Ghostwright's hosting accounts and tools. Ghostwright alone views
its hosting account. Partner may ask Ghostwright for performance information about a Site, and Ghostwright will
provide it if possible.
3. Ordering, Greenlight, and delivery
3.1  A Client completes the Intake on Partner's subdomain, and the answers reach Ghostwright by email. Sending
a Client to the Intake is Partner's order for a Site. If Partner did not authorize a completed Intake, Partner must tell
Ghostwright within 2 Business Days after Ghostwright sends the Setup Fee invoice for it, and Ghostwright will
cancel that invoice. Ghostwright may copy Partner on each Intake it receives. Partner will point a subdomain of its
website to the Intake as Ghostwright instructs. The Intake includes the authorization confirmation described in
Section 12.3.
3.2
starts coding only after the Setup Fee is paid in full. That moment is the Greenlight.
3.3  Ghostwright will deliver the first version of the Site within 5 to 7 Business Days after Greenlight. If Partner or
the Client is late with content, answers, or access, the timeline moves back by the same number of days.
3.4  The Setup Fee is non-refundable once work begins. This applies even if Partner or the Client cancels, stops
responding, or never launches the Site.
3.5  If Partner or the Client does not respond for 30 consecutive days after Ghostwright's written request, the build
is treated as abandoned. Section 10.5 then applies to the work product.
4. Build revisions
4.1  Each Site includes two rounds of revisions after the first version is delivered.
4.2  The process is:
1.Ghostwright delivers version 1.
2.Partner sends one consolidated written list of requested changes.
3.Ghostwright delivers version 2 within 3 Business Days of receiving the list.
4.Partner may send one more consolidated list.
5.Ghostwright delivers version 3 within 3 Business Days. Version 3 is final.
Partner Service Agreement, Version 1.2
  When Ghostwright receives a complete Intake, it invoices the Setup Fee of $150 for that Site. Ghostwright

Page 3 of 12
4.3  A revision can include major changes to what Ghostwright already delivered, such as adding or removing
images, adding or removing services and their pages, and updating hours, contact details, text, colors, spacing,
and the layout of existing pages. New features, new integrations, and redesigns are not revisions and are quoted
separately.
4.4  Partner's feedback is due within 5 Business Days after each delivery. If Ghostwright receives none, that
version is treated as approved and Ghostwright proceeds to launch.
4.5  Feedback must come from Partner's authorized contacts listed in Exhibit B, not from the Client directly,
unless Partner has chosen a direct communication option under Section 9.6, in which case the Client may send
feedback directly with Partner copied.
4.6  A round is one consolidated list. Requests sent piecemeal count together as one round, and any new list after
a version is delivered counts as a new round.
4.7  Each additional round costs $75 flat. Ghostwright invoices it when the round is requested and starts work
once it is paid.
5. Launch, domain, and Go-Live
5.1  After Approval, Ghostwright schedules the launch. Launch requires access to the Client's domain settings.
5.2  The Client owns its domain and registers it in the Client's own account. Ghostwright gives Partner the exact
DNS records and instructions, and Partner is responsible for getting the Client to complete them. Partner may ask
Ghostwright for technical help with DNS, and Ghostwright will deal only with Partner, unless Partner has chosen a
direct communication option under Section 9.6. If the Client gives Ghostwright temporary access to its domain
registrar account for setup, Section 14.5 applies.
5.3  Before launch, Ghostwright hosts a private preview of the Site at no charge.
5.4  If launch is delayed more than 14 days after Approval for reasons outside Ghostwright's control (for example,
the Client has not given domain access), the Billing Start Date is the 15th day after Approval, even though
Go-Live has not happened. The Monthly Fee then starts under Section 6.3.
5.5  Launch Checklist. Before Go-Live, Ghostwright will:
•
submit a test through each contact form and confirm the message reaches the intended recipient address;
•
ask Partner (or the Client through Partner) to confirm that the test message was received; and
•
email Partner the Launch Checklist, a short list of the tests it ran and the results.
Partner will confirm the Launch Checklist by replying to that email within 2 Business Days after Ghostwright
sends it. If Ghostwright receives no reply in that time, Ghostwright may launch and the checklist is treated as
confirmed. The completed Launch Checklist is the record of what was working at launch.
6. Fees and payment
6.1  Partner pays the Setup Fee for each Site and the Monthly Fee for each Active Site, as set out in Exhibit A.
6.2  The Setup Fee is invoiced when Ghostwright receives a complete Intake and is due before work begins.
6.3  The Monthly Fee starts on the first day of the calendar month after the Billing Start Date. Ghostwright does
not charge for the partial month in which the Billing Start Date falls.
6.4  Ghostwright sends Partner one bundled invoice on the 1st of each month, through Wave or a successor tool.
The invoice lists each Active Site whose Monthly Fee has started and covers that month. It is due by the 8th.
6.5  Ghostwright may offer card or bank autopay. Payment methods and any other payment details are stated on
each invoice.
Partner Service Agreement, Version 1.2

Page 4 of 12
6.6  If an invoice is not paid by the 15th, Partner owes a flat late fee of $15 per invoice, not per Site. Ghostwright
may send automatic reminders.
6.7  If an invoice is still unpaid 30 days after its due date, Ghostwright will send Partner written notice. Five days
after that notice, Ghostwright may suspend the Sites on that invoice until it is paid. If it is still unpaid 60 days after
its due date, those Sites are treated as cancelled under Section 11.
6.8  Partner is responsible for telling its Clients about any suspension. Ghostwright is not liable for losses caused
by a suspension made under Section 6.7.
6.9  Ghostwright may change the Monthly Fee for future months on 30 days' written notice. Setup Fees for Sites
already greenlit do not change. The new fee applies starting with the first monthly invoice under Section 6.4 that is
dated at least 30 days after the notice takes effect under Section 16.4. If Partner objects, it may cancel affected
Sites by written notice that Ghostwright receives before that invoice date, and Ghostwright will not invoice the new
fee for those Sites.
6.10  Fees exclude taxes. If Ghostwright is required to collect any sales, use, or transaction privilege tax, Partner
will pay it. Partner is responsible for taxes on its own resale of the Sites.
6.11  If Partner disputes an invoice, it must tell Ghostwright before the due date and pay the undisputed part.
Section 7 covers unpaid Client accounts.
6.12  Any credit Ghostwright owes Partner under this Agreement (including under Section 8.14) is applied against
Partner's next invoice.
7. Clients who do not pay Partner
7.1  Partner is responsible for collecting from its Clients. Partner remains responsible for the Setup Fee of every
Site it greenlights.
7.2  If a Client has not paid Partner for a Site, Partner may tell Ghostwright in writing, before the invoice due date,
which Site and Client are unpaid. Ghostwright will then remove that Site's Monthly Fee from the current invoice. If
the invoice is already paid, Ghostwright will credit the amount to the next invoice or refund it, at Ghostwright's
option.
7.3  The rest of the invoice stays due by its due date. The late fee in Section 6.6 applies only to the undisputed
amount.
7.4  The unpaid Site then follows the schedule in Section 6.7, counted from the invoice's original due date: written
notice to Partner at 30 days, suspension 5 days after that notice, and cancellation at 60 days. Partner is
responsible for telling the Client. If the Client pays Partner before cancellation, Partner pays the Monthly Fees that
were removed, and Ghostwright restores the Site.
7.5  Ghostwright may ask for reasonable confirmation of an unpaid Client. If Partner makes repeated or
unsupported claims, Ghostwright may end this right by written notice.
8. Support, content edits, and contact forms
Support and edits
8.1  The Monthly Fee covers hosting, SSL, infrastructure, technical support, and content edits for each Active
Site.
8.2  Content edits are changes to text, images, hours, service areas, and contact information. After launch,
Ghostwright will use reasonable efforts to complete a content edit within 2 to 3 Business Days after receiving a
complete request from Partner. This is a target, not a guarantee. If a request is unclear or Ghostwright needs
more information, the target starts when Ghostwright has what it needs.
Partner Service Agreement, Version 1.2

Page 5 of 12
8.3  Larger work, such as a redesign, is not a content edit and is quoted separately. Once Partner accepts the
quote, pays any amount due before work starts, and Ghostwright has what it needs, Ghostwright will use
reasonable efforts to complete a redesign within 3 to 5 Business Days. Ghostwright may state a different timeline
in the quote for unusually large work. These timelines are targets, not guarantees.
8.4  New major service pages, new features and integrations (other than simple tracking), and redesigns are not
content edits. Ghostwright quotes them separately. Simple tracking is included in the Monthly Fee and is handled
as a content edit. It means adding a standard tracking tag or conversion snippet that the Client's own account
provides, such as Google Ads conversion tracking, Google Analytics, or a Meta Pixel. Ghostwright installs the tag
the Client supplies. Partner and the Client are responsible for the tracking account, the ad platform's rules, what
the tag collects, and any privacy notice or consent it requires, and Ghostwright does not promise that the tracking
will report accurately. Custom event setups, tag-manager or server-side configurations, consent banners, and
integrations with other systems are not simple tracking and are quoted separately.
8.5  Requests must come from Partner's authorized contacts listed in Exhibit B. Ghostwright does not take
requests from Clients, unless Partner has chosen a direct communication option under Section 9.6.
8.6  Ghostwright will use commercially reasonable efforts to keep each Site online but does not guarantee uptime.
Outages of third-party services, and short maintenance windows, are not a breach.
8.7  Ghostwright does not monitor the Client's domain registrar account, EmailJS account, or other Client
accounts after launch, and may not know if one has a problem or is compromised.
8.8  Prompt notice. Partner will tell Ghostwright as soon as it learns of any problem with a Site, including a form
that is not delivering messages, a Site that is down or displaying incorrectly, wrong or outdated information, a limit
or billing problem on a Client account, or a suspected compromise of any account connected to a Site. Partner will
send the notice by email to Ghostwright's notice address in Exhibit B. Quick notice lets Ghostwright fix problems
sooner and protects the Client's experience. Where this Agreement ties a remedy to a problem, a delay in giving
notice can reduce or end that remedy to the extent the delay made the problem worse.
Contact forms and EmailJS
8.9  Every contact form on a Site uses EmailJS.
8.10  The Client, through Partner, creates and owns the EmailJS account. Ghostwright either uses temporary
access to set up the forms or gives Partner written setup instructions. Ghostwright uses any access only for setup
and does not keep the credentials. Partner or the Client may change or revoke access at any time.
8.11  Standard setup. Ghostwright includes a honeypot spam field and a submission cooldown on each contact
form.
8.12  Partner and the Client are responsible for the EmailJS account, including its plan, usage limits, billing,
upgrades before a limit is reached, recipient addresses, settings, and security. EmailJS sets its own limits, prices,
and terms, and may change them. Partner and the Client will keep the account and its billing and recipient details
current.
8.13  Ghostwright is not responsible if a form stops working or is limited for a reason outside Ghostwright's code
and configuration. Examples include reaching a plan limit, a plan or price change, an account suspension or
lapse, a wrong or outdated recipient address, a change to or discontinuation of EmailJS's service, a compromised
account, and spam that gets past the standard setup in Section 8.11.
8.14  Ghostwright is responsible for a Ghostwright-Caused Form Failure, meaning a form failure caused by an
error in code or configuration that Ghostwright wrote or set up, such as a form that sends submissions repeatedly
or sends them to the wrong recipient. For a Ghostwright-Caused Form Failure, Ghostwright will:
•
correct the error at no charge; and
Partner Service Agreement, Version 1.2

