14. Confidentiality, data, and security
14.1  Each party will keep the other's confidential information private and use it only to carry out this Agreement.
Confidential information includes the terms of this Agreement and Partner's pricing and margins. It does not
include information that is public, already known, or independently developed.
14.2  Form submissions. Contact-form submissions are sent through EmailJS to the recipient address in the
Client's EmailJS account. Ghostwright does not receive submissions from a Site's contact forms. They go directly
to the Client's recipient address and do not pass through or remain in Ghostwright's systems, email, logs, or
backups. The Intake is different (see Section 14.3). EmailJS and any other provider may store message content,
logs, or attachments under their own terms and the Client's account settings. Partner and the Client are
responsible for those settings and for their own retention of submissions. Files delivered through a form to the
Client belong to the Client. If Ghostwright receives submission data by accident, it will delete it within 30 days and
will not use it.
14.3  Ghostwright receives each Intake by email through its own EmailJS account. Files uploaded with an Intake
are stored with Ghostwright's file-storage provider under random file names, and Ghostwright deletes them about
90 days after Go-Live, other than material the Site itself uses. Ghostwright will use personal information in Intakes
to build and maintain Sites. It will not sell it, will protect it with reasonable security, and may share it with vendors it
needs (such as hosting and form tools). Partner is responsible for any consents it needs from its Clients.
14.4  Within 60 days after a Site is cancelled or this Agreement ends, and on Partner's request, Ghostwright will
delete Client personal data it holds. Exceptions are records it must keep for legal or billing reasons and the
backup described in Section 11.9.
14.5  Accounts and credentials. The Client owns and controls its domain registrar account and its EmailJS
account. Ghostwright may receive temporary access to either one, only for setup. Ghostwright will protect any
credentials it receives, use them only for setup, and not keep them longer than needed. Partner and the Client will
change or revoke temporary access when it is no longer needed. Each party protects the credentials it controls.
14.6  Suspected compromise. If either party learns or suspects that a credential or account connected to a Site
has been compromised, it will tell the other by email as soon as it can. If Ghostwright learns of a security incident
affecting Client data, it will tell Partner within 72 hours. Ghostwright investigates and fixes a compromise caused
by Ghostwright's own error at no charge. Other investigation or remediation work is quoted separately.
15. Term and termination
15.1  This Agreement starts on the Effective Date and continues until terminated. There is no minimum term or
minimum volume.
15.2  Partner may end this Agreement on 30 days' written notice. Sites stay online until the notice period ends,
unless Partner cancels them earlier under Section 11.
15.3  Ghostwright may end this Agreement, without cause, on 60 days' written notice. Sites stay online through
that period, and Partner may complete the Buyout Steps for any Site during it under Section 11.10.
15.4  Either party may end this Agreement if the other materially breaches it and does not fix the breach within 15
days after written notice. Ghostwright may also end it for non-payment as described in Section 6.7.
